<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Unsuri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1040</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Unsuri was a Persian poet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a> who became the poet laureate, or king of poets, at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a>. He wrote panegyric odes celebrating Mahmud's victories and also verse romances, now mostly lost. He was regarded by contemporaries and later critics as the foremost master of the Persian court ode of his age.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unsuri.jpg" alt="Unsuri" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Poets_Firdawsi,_%27Unsuri,_and_%27Asjadi_-_Walters_W6032B_-_Full_Page.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
